# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Retry a failed run, and reuse its samples {#retry-a-failed-run-and-reuse-its-samples}"
msgstr "Retry run yang gagal, dan pakai ulang sample-nya {#retry-a-failed-run-and-reuse-its-samples}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Retry:** Suppose that, in a run with **Max Iteration** set to `10`, a solver job hits its walltime in round 5 and `sqd_loop` fails. Raise the walltime in the `exec-sqd-fulqrum-slurm` block under **Blocks**, then select **Retry** on the failed flow run. The retried run loads the stored results of the first three stages and submits no QPU job. It runs only `sqd_loop` again, with the new walltime, and starts at round 5 from the checkpoint of round 4. Its log shows `[ckpt] RESUME from …: completed 4 step(s)`, then `SQD iteration 5/10`, as in the following image.\n"
msgstr "**Retry:** Misalkan, di run dengan **Max Iteration** diatur ke `10`, sebuah job solver mencapai walltime-nya di putaran 5 dan `sqd_loop` gagal. Naikkan walltime di block `exec-sqd-fulqrum-slurm` di bawah **Blocks**, lalu pilih **Retry** pada flow run yang gagal. Run yang di-retry memuat hasil tersimpan dari tiga tahap pertama dan tidak mengirim job QPU. Run ini hanya menjalankan `sqd_loop` lagi, dengan walltime baru, dan mulai di putaran 5 dari checkpoint putaran 4. Lognya menampilkan `[ckpt] RESUME from …: completed 4 step(s)`, lalu `SQD iteration 5/10`, seperti pada gambar berikut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Reuse:** A new run computes everything again unless you point it to earlier samples. To try another subspace dimension with the same samples, start a custom run with the same parameters, set **Load from QRMI Job Directory** (`qrmi_result_dir`) to the work directory in the `sqd-sampling-source` artifact of the first run, and change **Subspace Dimension**. The new run replaces `get_lucj_params` and `quantum_sampling` with `load_qrmi_result`, which reads the samples and submits nothing to the QPU. **Reset Mitigation** in `sqd-advanced-settings` must match the first run, because the reload applies it. For samples taken through IQP, set **Load from Qiskit Runtime Job ID** (`qiskit_runtime_job_id`) instead, and the stage is `load_runtime_job`. It reads the job with the credentials of the prefect-qiskit `QuantumRuntime` block named in **Quantum Runtime Block (reload)** (`ibm-runner` by default). Create that block one time with `prefect block create quantum-runtime`.\n"
msgstr "**Reuse:** Run baru menghitung ulang semuanya kecuali kamu mengarahkannya ke sample sebelumnya. Untuk mencoba dimensi subruang lain dengan sample yang sama, mulai custom run dengan parameter yang sama, atur **Load from QRMI Job Directory** (`qrmi_result_dir`) ke direktori kerja di artifact `sqd-sampling-source` dari run pertama, lalu ubah **Subspace Dimension**. Run baru menggantikan `get_lucj_params` dan `quantum_sampling` dengan `load_qrmi_result`, yang membaca sample dan tidak mengirim apa pun ke QPU. **Reset Mitigation** di `sqd-advanced-settings` harus sama dengan run pertama, karena proses reload menerapkannya. Untuk sample yang diambil lewat IQP, atur **Load from Qiskit Runtime Job ID** (`qiskit_runtime_job_id`) sebagai gantinya, dan tahapnya adalah `load_runtime_job`. Tahap ini membaca job dengan kredensial dari block `QuantumRuntime` prefect-qiskit yang disebut di **Quantum Runtime Block (reload)** (`ibm-runner` secara default). Buat block itu sekali dengan `prefect block create quantum-runtime`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Continue a recovery with more rounds:** Start a custom run with the same parameters, set **Resume from Checkpoint** (`resume_checkpoint`) to the path in the `sqd-checkpoint` artifact of the first run, and raise **Max Iteration**. The new run continues after the completed rounds, from the stored occupancies and best energy. For example, a checkpoint with 32 of 100 rounds done and **Max Iteration** set to `200` continues at round 33/200. The new run reads that checkpoint and writes its own, and the following rules apply.\n"
msgstr "**Lanjutkan recovery dengan lebih banyak putaran:** Mulai custom run dengan parameter yang sama, atur **Resume from Checkpoint** (`resume_checkpoint`) ke path di artifact `sqd-checkpoint` dari run pertama, lalu naikkan **Max Iteration**. Run baru melanjutkan setelah putaran yang sudah selesai, dari okupansi dan energi terbaik yang tersimpan. Misalnya, checkpoint dengan 32 dari 100 putaran selesai dan **Max Iteration** diatur ke `200` melanjutkan di putaran 33/200. Run baru membaca checkpoint itu dan menulis checkpoint-nya sendiri, dan aturan berikut berlaku.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The samples, the molecule, **Subspace Dimension**, **Batch Number**, and the solver type (the `fulqrum_solver_job` part of the solver block) must match the first run, so reuse its samples as in **Reuse**.\n"
msgstr "Sample, molekul, **Subspace Dimension**, **Batch Number**, dan tipe solver (bagian `fulqrum_solver_job` dari solver block) harus sama dengan run pertama, jadi pakai ulang sample-nya seperti di **Reuse**.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The name and the job settings of the solver block, such as its walltime, can change.\n"
msgstr "Nama dan pengaturan job dari solver block, seperti walltime-nya, boleh berubah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a setting that must match differs, the run fails before any solver job and names the difference.\n"
msgstr "Kalau ada pengaturan yang harus sama tapi berbeda, run gagal sebelum job solver apa pun dan menyebutkan perbedaannya.\n"

